# SnapScreen

**A dedicated touch control panel for Snapmaker U1.**

SnapScreen brings printer control, live monitoring and advanced G-code tools
into one fast, purpose-built interface. It is designed for daily use at the
printer: clear at a glance, responsive to touch and useful from the first layer
to the finished print.

[Download the latest firmware](https://github.com/AlphaStudioDE/SnapScreen/releases/latest)
| [Report a problem](https://github.com/AlphaStudioDE/SnapScreen/issues)
| [Support development](https://buymeacoffee.com/damianborkh)

## At a glance

- Live printer status, temperatures, progress and Smart ETA
- Dedicated controls for movement, heating, extrusion, fans and tuning
- Print file browser with thumbnails and useful file information
- Interactive 2D and 3D print previews
- Full G-code Viewer with layer navigation, feature filters and tool colors
- Live camera view with touch pan, smooth zoom and fullscreen mode
- Bed Mesh visualization and guided calibration tools
- G-code terminal, custom macros and configurable dashboard widgets
- Twelve visual styles, each available in Light and Dark mode
- Built-in OTA firmware updates
- Separate firmware builds for SnapScreen Standard and SnapScreen XL

## Built around the print

### Monitor and control

The Status and Printing views keep the information that matters close at hand:
the active file, print state, tool and bed temperatures, progress, remaining
time, flow, speed and fan controls. The dashboard can be arranged around the
way each user works.

### See the model before and during printing

SnapScreen can show the slicer's 2D thumbnail immediately and build an
interactive 3D representation from the selected G-code. The G-code Viewer adds
layer controls, movement and extrusion visibility, feature filtering, tool
colors, camera controls and detailed file statistics.

### Work directly with printer files

Browse files stored on the printer, inspect thumbnails and metadata, select a
job and start working without moving back to a computer. Preview data is loaded
in the background and retained where practical so changing screens does not
needlessly restart the work.

### Camera, calibration and diagnostics

The camera view supports touch-driven framing, zoom and fullscreen viewing.
Bed Mesh tools provide both 2D and 3D inspection, while the terminal and macro
screens remain available for experienced users and troubleshooting.

## Appearance

SnapScreen includes twelve distinct interface styles:

`Signature` | `Precision` | `Studio` | `Signal` | `Porcelain` | `Workbench` |
`Editorial` | `Technical` | `Contrast` | `Outline` | `Paper` | `Facet`

Every style has independent Light and Dark variants. The selected appearance is
stored on the device and does not alter printer settings or dashboard layouts.

## Hardware variants

| Variant | Display | Release file |
| --- | --- | --- |
| SnapScreen Standard | 800 x 480 | `firmware.bin` |
| SnapScreen XL | 1024 x 600 | `firmwarexl.bin` |

Always use the firmware that matches the hardware variant. Existing devices can
receive supported releases through SnapScreen's built-in OTA updater.

## Multi-material development

SnapScreen includes the foundation for expanded multi-material workflows and
integration with the Rainbow toolchain. CFS Nano support is currently
**experimental** and remains under hardware and protocol validation. It should
not yet be treated as production-ready changer control.

## Releases

Release packages contain:

| Asset | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `firmware.bin` | Firmware for SnapScreen Standard |
| `firmwarexl.bin` | Firmware for SnapScreen XL |
| `version.json` | OTA release manifest |

Read the notes attached to each release before updating. They include the
visible changes, compatibility notes, validation performed and any known
limitations.

**Latest release:** [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/AlphaStudioDE/SnapScreen/releases/latest)

## Feedback and bug reports

Real hardware reports are invaluable. When reporting a problem, please include:

- SnapScreen hardware variant
- firmware version
- steps needed to reproduce the behavior
- a photo or screenshot when the issue is visual
- serial logs when available
- the relevant G-code file for preview or viewer problems

Please do not publish passwords, Wi-Fi credentials, activation data or other
private information in an issue.

## Project status

SnapScreen is actively developed and tested on physical Standard and XL
hardware. Some integrations are experimental and are identified as such in the
release notes. This is an independent community project and is not affiliated
with or endorsed by Snapmaker.

